    "reported_result": {
      "url": "https://chile.travel/en/destinations/san-pedro-de-atacama/",
      "http_status": 200,
      "excerpt": "NE - OUTDOOR LIFE Updated on 10 de February, 2026 The Oasis of the Atacama Desert San Pedro de Atacama is the gateway to the world&#8217;s driest desert. From here, you can discover some of northern Chile&#8217;s most stunning landscapes, where geography and time seem to stand still. In the Moon Valley, you&#8217;ll feel like you&#8217;re on another planet, while at the Tatio Geysers, you&#8217;ll discover the Earth&#8217;s power in full activity. You can also explore lagoons and salt flats of great biodiversity, home to flamingos and birds adapted to extreme aridity. And when night falls, stargazing will allow you to observe one of the clearest skies on the planet. San Pedro de Atacama --> Unmissable of San Pedro de Atacama See all the attractions Desert and Altiplano Tatio Geysers Desert and Altiplano ALMA Observatory Desert and Altiplano Piedras Rojas (Red Stones) Desert and Altiplano Los Flamencos National Reserve Desert and Altiplano Valle de la Luna (Moon Valley) Desert and Altiplano Puritama Hot Springs Desert and Altiplano Hidden Lagoons of Baltinache Desert and Altiplano Altiplanic Lagoons See all the attractions Discover trends on our blog Must read 23 Oct 2026 New Year 2027 in Chile! Celebrate in our urban, natural, and coastal destinations 21 Oct 2026 From the Desert to the Glaciers: How to Combine Atacama and Patagonia in a Single Trip 13 Oct 2026 We&#039;re champions! Chile triumphs in four categories at the 2026 South America &quot;Oscars of Tourism&quot; 17 Aug 2026 Travel Backpack: What to Pack for Your Chile Trip to Avoid Overpaying 13 Aug 2026 7 Chilean Salt Flats That Will Amaze You, and How to Visit Them 10 Aug 2026 What to do in Chile: From the Atacama Desert to Patagonia 5 Aug 2026 Vozinha Arrives in Chile: The Landscapes Awaiting the World Cup Star Goalkeeper 22 Jul 2026 Tulor Village: The Atacama Village Hidden for 1,700 Years Under the Sand Plan your trip to San Pedro de Atacama Suggested route Calculating route... 1 Santiago 2 San Pedro de Atacama How to get there How to get there by air Fly to El Loa Airport in Calama (CJC), with direct flights from Santiago. From there, you must travel 100 km (1 hour 30 minutes) along Route 23. Another option is Antofagasta Airport (ANF), located 315 km (4 hours) away. How to get there by land From Santiago, you must drive along Route 5 North (1,530 km, 22 hours) to Calama, a trip that you should plan in several stages. From Calama, the final stretch is 100 km along Route 23 (1 hour 30 minutes), which you can do by bus, transfer, or private vehicle. Must-Know Tips Bring light clothing for the day and warm clothing for the cold nights. The altitude can affect you, so hydrate well and rest upon arrival. In summer, book in advance due to high demand, while in winter temperatures drop considerably, a fundamental aspect if you are going to take a night tour. Discover destinations near San Pedro de Atacama Other incredible destinations in the same area Bahía Inglesa La Serena and Coquimbo Route of the Missions Elqui Valley Arica Iquique Itineraries that include San Pedro de Atacama Recommended routes that pass through this destination. See all itineraries Chile in 8 days: from Santiago to the Atacama Desert. 8 days > 7 attractions Tatio Geysers Valle de la Luna (Moon Valley) Cerro San Cristóbal Gastronomic Neighborhoods • Wine Routes and Gastronomy Adventure in Guatín and the Cactus Valley 2 days > 1 attraction Puritama Hot Springs Nature and National Parks • Observation of Flora, Fauna, and Landscapes Santiago, Desert, and Patag",
